### wallet-service smoke requests
###
### An executable tour of the generated HTTP surface, in the order a reviewer
### would exercise it. Run the application first: `sh run.sh app`.
###
### Supported by the REST Client extension in VS Code and by the HTTP client in
### IntelliJ IDEA. Requests are separated by `###`; send them one at a time.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Liveness - should report status UP
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health
Accept: application/json

### OpenAPI specification - the contract the requests below follow
GET {{baseUrl}}/v3/api-docs
Accept: application/json

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Wallet
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Create a Wallet
POST {{baseUrl}}/wallets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111112",
  "balance": 124.45
}

### List active Wallet records, paged and sorted
GET {{baseUrl}}/wallets?page=0&size=20
Accept: application/json

### Read one active Wallet
GET {{baseUrl}}/wallets/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111112
Accept: application/json

### Replace a Wallet
PUT {{baseUrl}}/wallets/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111112
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111113",
  "balance": 125.45
}

### Partially update a Wallet - omitted fields are left untouched
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/wallets/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111112
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "balance": 125.45
}

### Soft delete a Wallet - the row survives as a tombstone
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/wallets/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111112

### List soft-deleted Wallet records
GET {{baseUrl}}/wallets/deleted
Accept: application/json

### Read one soft-deleted Wallet
GET {{baseUrl}}/wallets/deleted/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111112
Accept: application/json

### Restore a soft-deleted Wallet
POST {{baseUrl}}/wallets/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111112/restore

